rows, beard or body hair and may fluctuate over time.", "approach": "Treatment depends on the number, size and location of patches and the overall course.", "slug": "alopecia-areata"}, {"category": "Hair & Scalp", "title": "Premature Greying", "summary": "Earlier-than-expected loss of natural hair pigment.", "detail": "Premature greying can have genetic, nutritional or other associations, although many cases are familial.", "approach": "A consultation can determine whether any associated issue needs attention; cosmetic options can also be discussed.", "slug": "premature-greying"}, {"category": "Hair & Scalp", "title": "Dandruff & Scalp Scaling", "summary": "Scalp flaking associated with dandruff, seborrheic dermatitis or other scalp conditions.", "detail": "Persistent scaling can also occur with psoriasis, fungal disease or contact reactions.", "approach": "Diagnosis helps choose the correct scalp treatment rather than treating every type of flaking the same way.", "slug": "dandruff-scalp-scaling"}, {"category": "Hair & Scalp", "title": "Itchy Scalp", "summary": "Scalp itching with multiple possible dermatological causes.", "detail": "Itching can accompany dandruff, dermatitis, psoriasis, infection, allergy or excessive dryness.", "approach": "The scalp is examined for redness, scale, lesions or hair changes before treatment is selected.", "slug": "itchy-scalp"}, {"category": "Hair & Scalp", "title": "Scalp Psoriasis", "summary": "Psoriasis involving the scalp, often causing thick scale and well-defined plaques.", "detail": "Scalp psoriasis can extend beyond the hairline and may be mistaken for severe dandruff.", "approach": "Treatment focuses on controlling inflammation and scale and maintaining the scalp between flares.", "slug": "scalp-psoriasis"}, {"category": "Hair & Scalp", "title": "Traction Alopecia", "summary": "Hair loss caused by repeated pulling or tension on the hair.", "detail": "Tight hairstyles, extensions and repeated traction can damage follicles, 